"The newest Wi-Fi generation the AP supports (inferred from its information elements). Newer generations are faster and handle many devices better; actual speed also depends on the client." = "AP 支持的最高 Wi-Fi 代际（由广播的信息元素推断）。代际越新，速率和多设备效率越高；实际速率还取决于终端是否支持。";
"Latest" = "最新";
"Mainstream" = "主流";
"Adequate" = "够用";
"n (Wi-Fi 4) or older" = "n (Wi-Fi 4) 及更早";
"Legacy; slows down the whole channel" = "老旧，会拖慢同信道";
"The country code broadcast by the AP; it determines the allowed channels and maximum transmit power." = "AP 广播的国家码，决定可用信道和最大发射功率。";
"Infrastructure = a regular router/AP. Ad-hoc (IBSS) = devices connected directly to each other; rare." = "基础设施 = 普通路由器/AP；点对点 (IBSS) = 设备之间直连的 ad-hoc 网络，少见。";
"2.4 GHz penetrates walls and reaches far, but has only 3 non-overlapping channels (1/6/11) and lots of interference. 5 GHz has more channels and is faster but weaker through walls. 6 GHz is the cleanest and fastest with the shortest range, and needs Wi-Fi 6E or newer devices." = "2.4 GHz 穿墙好、覆盖远，但只有 3 个不重叠信道（1/6/11），干扰多；5 GHz 信道多、速度快，穿墙较弱；6 GHz 最干净、最快，覆盖最短，需要 Wi-Fi 6E 以上设备。";
"The 20 MHz channel the AP sends beacons on. On 2.4 GHz only 1 / 6 / 11 should be used; other channels interfere with both neighbors." = "AP 发信标所在的 20 MHz 信道。2.4 GHz 应只用 1 / 6 / 11，其他信道会同时干扰两边。";
"The center of the bonded 40/80/160 MHz channel; the spectrum chart is drawn around it. For 2.4 GHz 40 MHz the extension direction is unavailable, so it is estimated." = "多个 20 MHz 信道绑定成 40/80/160 MHz 后的中心位置，频谱图按它来画。2.4 GHz 的 40 MHz 拿不到扩展方向，是估算值。";
"The center frequency of the primary channel." = "主信道的中心频率。";
"The frequency range actually occupied given the channel width. APs whose ranges overlap interfere with each other." = "按带宽算出的实际占用频率范围，和别的 AP 有交叠就会互相干扰。";
"Wider channels give higher theoretical speed but overlap neighbors more easily and tolerate interference worse." = "带宽越宽理论速率越高，但更容易和邻居重叠、抗干扰更差。";
"20 MHz recommended" = "建议 20 MHz";
"80 MHz typical; 40 MHz when crowded" = "80 MHz 常用；拥挤时 40 MHz";
"160 MHz is common too" = "160 MHz 也很常见";
"How often the AP broadcasts beacons; 1 TU = 1.024 ms. The default of 100 TU almost never needs changing; too small wastes airtime, too large hurts discovery and power-save wakeups." = "AP 广播信标的周期，1 TU = 1.024 ms。默认 100 TU，几乎所有设备都不需要改；过小浪费空口，过大影响终端发现和省电唤醒。";
"RSSI, the received AP signal power in dBm; closer to 0 is stronger. Every 3 dB is a doubling of power." = "RSSI，接收到的 AP 信号功率，单位 dBm，越接近 0 越强。每差 3 dB 功率差一倍。";
"Excellent: full speed" = "优秀：满速";
"Good: video calls and 4K are fine" = "良好：视频会议、4K 都没问题";
"Fair: fine for browsing, slower speeds" = "一般：日常上网可以，速率下降";
"Weak: stutters and slowdowns" = "较弱：容易卡顿、掉速";
"Poor: frequent disconnects" = "很差：经常断连";
"Background noise on the channel; lower (more negative) is better. CoreWLAN only measures the connected network; others show “—”." = "该信道上的背景噪声，越低（越负）越好。CoreWLAN 只测当前连接的网络，其他网络显示“—”。";
"Quiet" = "安静";
"Some interference" = "有一定干扰";
"Noisy (microwaves, Bluetooth, wireless cameras, …)" = "噪声大（微波炉、蓝牙、无线摄像头等）";
"SNR = signal strength − noise. It reflects real-world experience better than signal alone: a strong signal with high noise still won't be fast. Only available for the connected network." = "SNR = 信号强度 − 噪声，比单看信号更能反映实际体验：信号再强、噪声也高，速率照样上不去。只有当前连接的网络能算。";
"Excellent: highest modulation rates" = "优秀：可跑最高调制速率";
"Good" = "良好";
"Fair: noticeably slower" = "一般：速率明显下降";
"Poor: unstable" = "较差：不稳定";
"Very poor: barely connects" = "很差：基本连不上";
"Min / average / max signal sampled over the last 5 minutes of this session. A spread over 10 dB means the signal is unstable (people moving, obstructions, AP power changes, …)." = "本次运行期间最近 5 分钟采到的信号最低/平均/最高值。最高和最低相差超过 10 dB 说明信号不稳定（人员走动、遮挡、AP 调功率等）。";
"When this BSSID was first seen in this session." = "本次运行中第一次扫描到这个 BSSID 的时间。";
"Other APs on the same primary channel. Co-channel APs take turns using the air (CSMA/CA); if they can hear each other they queue, so the more there are, the less airtime each gets." = "主信道相同的其他 AP。同信道的 AP 会轮流占用空口（CSMA/CA），能互相听到就要排队，数量越多每个人分到的时间越少。";
"Idle" = "空闲";
"Somewhat crowded" = "有些拥挤";
"Crowded; consider changing channel" = "拥挤，考虑换信道";
"APs whose occupied frequencies overlap (including co-channel). Partial overlap is worse than sharing a channel: the APs can't coordinate and just see each other as noise." = "占用频率有交叠的 AP（含同信道）。部分重叠比同信道更糟：彼此无法正常协调，只能当噪声硬扛。";
"The number of associated clients the AP reports in its BSS Load element. Many home routers don't broadcast it." = "AP 在 BSS Load 信息里自报的已关联终端数。很多家用路由器不广播。";
